  <para style="q2">and Israel will be ashamed of his counsel.
<verse eid="HOS 10:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 10:7"/>Samaria—its king will be ended,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a splinter on the face of the waters.
<verse eid="HOS 10:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 10:8"/>And the high places of Aven will be destroyed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the sin of Israel.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Thorn and thistle will grow up on their altars,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will say to the mountains, “Cover us!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to the hills, “Fall on us!”

<verse eid="HOS 10:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 10:9"/>From the days of Gibeah
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have sinned, Israel.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There they have stood.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Will not war overtake them in Gibeah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">against the sons of injustice?
<verse eid="HOS 10:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 10:10"/>When it is my desire, I will chastise them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and peoples will be gathered against them
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they are bound to their two eyes.
<verse eid="HOS 10:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 10:11"/>And Ephraim {is} a trained heifer
</para>
  <para style="q2">loving to thresh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but I, I have passed over upon
</para>
  <para style="q2">the goodness of her neck.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will harness Ephraim;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Judah will plow;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Jacob will harrow by himself.

<verse eid="HOS 10:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 10:12"/>Sow for yourselves for righteousness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">reap to the mouth of covenant faithfulness.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Till for yourselves tillage,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {it is} time to seek Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">until he comes
</para>
  <para style="q2">and rains righteousness on you.
<verse eid="HOS 10:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 10:13"/>You have plowed wickedness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have reaped injustice.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have eaten the fruit of deception,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you trusted in your way,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the multitude of your warriors.
<verse eid="HOS 10:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 10:14"/>And a tumult will arise among your people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all your fortresses will be destroyed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">as Shalman destroyed Beth Arbel
</para>
  <para style="q2">on the day of battle—
</para>
  <para style="q1">a mother was dashed to pieces
</para>
  <para style="q2">upon {her} sons.
<verse eid="HOS 10:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HOS 10:15"/>Thus he will do to you, Bethel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the face of the evil of your evil.
</para>
  <para style="q1">At the dawn, the king of Israel being destroyed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">will be destroyed.


<verse eid="HOS 10:15"/><verse eid="HOS 10:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="HOS 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="HOS 11"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 11:1"/>When Israel was a child I loved him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and out of Egypt I called my son.
<verse eid="HOS 11:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 11:2"/>They called to them, thus they went from their faces.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They kept sacrificing to the Baals
</para>
  <para style="q2">and burning to the idols.
<verse eid="HOS 11:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 11:3"/>Yet I, I taught Ephraim to walk.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He took them upon his arms,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they did not know that I healed them.
<verse eid="HOS 11:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 11:4"/>I led them with cords of humanity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">with bands of love.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And I was to them like the lifters of a yoke on their jaws,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I bent down to him; I fed {him}.

<verse eid="HOS 11:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 11:5"/>He will not return to the land of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Assyria—he {will be} his king,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because they refused to return.
<verse eid="HOS 11:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 11:6"/>The sword will whirl against his cities,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will destroy his bars,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will devour because of their plans.
<verse eid="HOS 11:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 11:7"/>And my people are bent on turning away from me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Though they call to him on high,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will not raise {them} up at all.

<verse eid="HOS 11:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 11:8"/>How can I give you up, Ephraim,
</para>
  <para style="q2">surrender you, Israel?
</para>
  <para style="q1">How can I make you like Admah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">set you like Zeboiim?
</para>
  <para style="q1">My heart is turned over within me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all my compassions are aroused together.
<verse eid="HOS 11:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 11:9"/>I will not carry out the burning of my nose; I will not repeat to destroy Ephraim! For I {am} God and not man, the Holy {One} in your midst, and I will not come in wrath.

<verse eid="HOS 11:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 11:10"/>They will come after Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will roar like a lion.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When he, he roars,
</para>
  <para style="q2">sons will come trembling from the sea.
<verse eid="HOS 11:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 11:11"/>They will come trembling like a bird from Egypt, and like a dove from the land of Assyria. And I will settle them in their homes—the declaration of Yahweh.

<verse eid="HOS 11:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 11:12"/>Ephraim has surrounded me with lies, and the house of Israel with deceit. But Judah still roams with God, and is established with the Holy {One}.


<verse eid="HOS 11:12"/><verse eid="HOS 11:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="HOS 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="HOS 12"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 12:1"/>Ephraim is feeding on wind
</para>
  <para style="q2">and pursuing the east-wind all the day.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He multiplies lies and destruction.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And they cut a covenant with Assyria,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and oil is carried to Egypt.
<verse eid="HOS 12:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 12:2"/>And a dispute {is} to Yahweh with Judah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to punish Jacob according to his ways;
</para>
  <para style="q2">according to his deeds he will repay to him.
<verse eid="HOS 12:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 12:3"/>In the womb he took his brother by the heel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in his manhood he struggled with God.
<verse eid="HOS 12:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 12:4"/>And he struggled with an angel and prevailed.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He wept and begged favor of him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">At Bethel he found him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there he spoke with us.
<verse eid="HOS 12:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 12:5"/>And Yahweh, the God of Armies—
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh {is} his memorial name.
<verse eid="HOS 12:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 12:6"/>And you, by your God you must return.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Keep covenant faithfulness and justice,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and wait for your God continually.
<verse eid="HOS 12:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 12:7"/>A merchant—in his hand {are} scales of deceit—
</para>
  <para style="q2">he loves to oppress.
<verse eid="HOS 12:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 12:8"/>And Ephraim said, “Surely I have become rich;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have found wealth for myself.
</para>
  <para style="q1">All of my labors—they will not find iniquity in me
</para>
  <para style="q2">that {would be} sin.”
<verse eid="HOS 12:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 12:9"/>“And I {am} Yahweh your God from the land of Egypt.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will make you dwell in tents again,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as in the days of the appointed festival.
<verse eid="HOS 12:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 12:10"/>And I spoke through the prophets,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I, I multiplied visions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and by the hand of the prophets I gave parables.”
<verse eid="HOS 12:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 12:11"/>If Gilead {is} iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">surely they have become worthlessness.
</para>
  <para style="q1">In Gilgal, they sacrifice bulls;
</para>
  <para style="q2">even their altars {will be} like heaps
</para>
  <para style="q2">on the furrows of the field.
<verse eid="HOS 12:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 12:12"/>And Jacob fled {to} the field of Aram,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Israel served for a wife,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for a wife he kept
{sheep}.
<verse eid="HOS 12:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 12:13"/>And by a prophet Yahweh brought Israel up from Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and by a prophet he was kept.
<verse eid="HOS 12:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 12:14"/>Ephraim has provoked bitternesses,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his Lord will leave his bloodguilt on him
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will return his reproach to him.


<verse eid="HOS 12:14"/><verse eid="HOS 12:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="HOS 12"/>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="HOS 13"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 13:1"/>When Ephraim spoke—trembling!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He lifted up himself in Israel.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But he became guilty through Baal
</para>
  <para style="q2">and died.
<verse eid="HOS 13:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 13:2"/>And now they continue to sin,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they have made for themselves a cast image from their silver,
</para>
  <para style="q1">idols according to their skill,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of it the work of craftsmen.
</para>
  <para style="q1">To them they are saying {things},
</para>
  <para style="q2">the sacrificers of humanity, they kiss calves!

<verse eid="HOS 13:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 13:3"/>Therefore they will be like a cloud of the morning
</para>
  <para style="q2">and like the dew rising early, going;
</para>
  <para style="q1">like chaff—it is blown away from the threshing floor—
</para>
  <para style="q2">and like smoke from a window.

<verse eid="HOS 13:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 13:4"/>“Yet I {am} Yahweh your God from the land of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you will not know a god except me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is no savior besides me.
<verse eid="HOS 13:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 13:5"/>I, I knew you in the wilderness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the land of drought.
<verse eid="HOS 13:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 13:6"/>According to their pasturage, then they became satisfied;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they were satisfied, and their heart was lifted up.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Therefore they forgot me.

<verse eid="HOS 13:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 13:7"/>So I am to them like a lion;
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a leopard along the path I will watch.
<verse eid="HOS 13:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 13:8"/>I will encounter them like a bereaved bear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will tear open the enclosure of their heart.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And I will devour them there like a lioness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the beast of the field will rip them open.

<verse eid="HOS 13:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 13:9"/>It has destroyed you, Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that {you are} against me, against your help.
<verse eid="HOS 13:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HOS 13:10"/>Where {is} your king now,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that he may save you in all of your cities,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your judges of whom you said,
</para>
  <para style="q2">‘Give to me a king and princes’?
<verse eid="HOS 13:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HOS 13:11"/>I give to you a king in my nose,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I take
{him} away in my wrath.

<verse eid="HOS 13:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HOS 13:12"/>The iniquity of Ephraim {is} bound up;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his sin {is} stored up.
<verse eid="HOS 13:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="HOS 13:13"/>The pains of a woman giving birth will come to him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he {is} a son not wise,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for {at} the time he does not stand
</para>
  <para style="q2">at the womb opening of sons.

<verse eid="HOS 13:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HOS 13:14"/>From the hand of Sheol I would ransom them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from death I would redeem them!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Where are your plagues, Death?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Where is your destruction, Sheol?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Relenting is hidden from my eyes.

<verse eid="HOS 13:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HOS 13:15"/>Although he, among brothers, he bears fruit,
</para>
  <para style="q2">an easterly will come, the wind of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">coming up from the wilderness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his fountain will be ashamed
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his spring will dry up.
</para>
  <para style="q1">It, it will plunder the treasury
</para>
  <para style="q2">of every vessel of desire.

<verse eid="HOS 13:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HOS 13:16"/>Samaria will bear guilt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for she has rebelled against her God.
</para>
  <para style="q1">By the sword they will fall;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their young children will be dashed to pieces,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his pregnant women will be ripped open.”


<verse eid="HOS 13:16"/><verse eid="HOS 13:16"/></para>
  <chapter eid="HOS 13"/>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="HOS 14"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="HOS 14:1"/>Return, Israel, to Yahweh your God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you have stumbled in your iniquity.
<verse eid="HOS 14:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HOS 14:2"/>Take with you words and return to Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Say to him, “Take away all iniquity
</para>
  <para style="q2">and accept {what} is good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let us repay {with} bulls of our lips.
<verse eid="HOS 14:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HOS 14:3"/>Assyria will not save us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we will not ride on a horse.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And we will not say anymore, ‘Our God,’
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the work of our hands,
</para>
  <para style="q1">who by you the fatherless is shown compassion.”
<verse eid="HOS 14:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HOS 14:4"/>“I will heal their turning away;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will love them freely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for my nose has turned away from them.
<verse eid="HOS 14:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HOS 14:5"/>I will be like the dew to Israel;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will blossom like the lily,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will strike his roots like Lebanon.
<verse eid="HOS 14:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HOS 14:6"/>His shoots will go forth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his splendor will be like the olive tree,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the scent of him like Lebanon.”
<verse eid="HOS 14:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HOS 14:7"/>They will return, dwellers in his shadow;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will revive grain
</para>
  <para style="q2">and blossom like the vine.
</para>
  <para style="q1">His remembrance
{will be} like the wine of Lebanon.
<verse eid="HOS 14:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HOS 14:8"/>“Ephraim, what to me still to idols?
</para>
  <para style="q2">I, I have answered and I will look after him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I {am} like a luxuriant cypress;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from me your fruit is found.”
<verse eid="HOS 14:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HOS 14:9"/>Who {is} wise? Then let him understand these things.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Discerning? Then let him know them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">For the ways of Yahweh {are} right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the righteous will walk in them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the transgressors will stumble in them.
<verse eid="HOS 14:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="HOS 14"/>
</usx>
